lass=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">The user wants to share the HTML file with =
their client so the client can (1) open it on their phone and (2) make chan=
ges to it.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Practical constraints=
 to address:</div><ol start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto"=
>The client needs the file on their phone =E2=80=94 HTML files can be opene=
d on phones, but the easiest ways:</div><ul start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"p=
aragraph" dir=3D"auto">Send via WhatsApp/email =E2=80=94 but .html files vi=
a WhatsApp may not open directly; email attachments can be downloaded and o=
pened in a browser</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Host=
 it online (free options): GitHub Pages, Netlify Drop, Vercel, CodePen =E2=
=80=94 this is the BEST way for both viewing on phone AND making changes</d=
iv></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">For editing: GitHub (edit=
 code), CodePen/JSFiddle (online editor), or a local editor on phone</div><=
/li></ul></li></ol><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Key practical advi=
ce:</div><ul start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Easiest =
for client to view on phone: host it free online (Netlify Drop / GitHub Pag=
es / Vercel) =E2=86=92 gives a URL that works on any phone</div></li><li><d=
iv class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">For client to make changes:</div><ul st=
art=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Non-technical client: o=
nline editors like CodePen, or use a CMS-ish approach</div></li><li><div cl=
ass=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Technical client: GitHub repo =E2=86=92 they=
 can edit and the site auto-updates via GitHub Pages</div></li></ul></li></=
ul><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Let me give a clear step-by-step. =
I could also offer to help deploy. Actually, can I deploy it? No network ac=
cess in ipython. I can't deploy it myself. But I can give clear instruction=
s.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Should I use a widget? The in=
structions say consider widgets for interactive things. This is a how-to qu=
estion =E2=80=94 plain prose steps are fine. Keep it clear and structured.<=
/div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Two scenarios:
A. Just view on phone:</div><ol start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" di=
r=3D"auto">Email/WhatsApp the file =E2=80=94 on Android, download and open =
with browser; on iPhone it's trickier (needs an app or host)</div></li><li>=
<div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Better: host for free =E2=86=92 Netli=
fy Drop (drag &amp; drop, instant URL), no account even needed... actually =
Netlify Drop requires an account now. GitHub Pages requires account. Vercel=
 requires account. Tiiny.host is drag-drop, free tier, no account needed? T=
iiny.host free plan allows 1 site. Cloudflare Pages needs account.</div><ul=
 start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Simplest no-signup: =
tiiny.host (drag &amp; drop HTML =E2=86=92 get link)</div></li></ul></li><l=
i><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Phone hotspot same Wi-Fi: run a loc=
al server =E2=80=94 too technical for most clients.</div></li></ol><div cla=
ss=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">B. Client makes changes:</div><ul start=3D"1"=
><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Easiest no-code: edit via an onl=
ine editor</div><ul start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">C=
odePen: paste code, edit visually-ish</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph=
" dir=3D"auto">GitHub: if client knows code =E2=80=94 fork repo, edit, GitH=
ub Pages auto-deploys</div></li></ul></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=
=3D"auto">On-phone editing is painful; recommend editing on desktop, viewin=
g link on phone</div></li></ul><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Realis=
tic recommendation flow:</div><ol start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" =
dir=3D"auto">Host it: Netlify Drop (app.netlify.com/drop) =E2=80=94 drag th=
e html file, get a live URL like <a data-v-048cb31c=3D"" target=3D"_blank" =
href=3D"https://random-name.netlify.app/" rel=3D"noreferrer nofollow noopen=
er">https://random-name.netlify.app</a> that opens on any phone instantly. =
Free, and changes: drag new version or use Netlify's deploys.</div></li><li=
><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">For changes:</div><ul start=3D"1"><l=
i><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">If client is technical: put the fil=
e in a GitHub repo =E2=86=92 enable GitHub Pages =E2=86=92 free URL; they e=
dit code on github.com (even from phone browser, though awkward) and change=
s go live.</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">If client is=
 non-technical: have the client send you the changes; you edit and re-deplo=
y. Or use an online editor.</div></li></ul></li></ol><div class=3D"paragrap=
h" dir=3D"auto">Also mention: WhatsApp can't reliably open .html on iPhone;=
 avoid just sending the raw file.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto=
">Let me write a concise, structured answer. Not too long. Maybe use number=
ed steps. No need for tool calls =E2=80=94 this is pure advice. Keep it pla=
in prose with minimal markdown, though a couple of short lists genuinely he=
lp here.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Format: short intro, th=
en Option A (just view) and Option B (view + edit), then a recommendation. =
Keep it tight.</div></div></div></div></div> <div class=3D"scroll-edge-fade=
 scroll-edge-fade-bottom" aria-hidden=3D"true"></div><div class=3D"scroll-e=
