31c=3D"" class=3D"markdown"><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Good ques=
tion =E2=80=94 a raw <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=
=3D"segment-code-inline">.html</code> file is annoying to open on a phone (=
especially iPhone), so the trick is to <strong>host it online for free</str=
ong>. That gives your client a normal link (like <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D""=
 data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">https://something.netli=
fy.app</code>) that opens in any phone browser, and it also makes future ed=
its easy.</div><h2 class=3D"">Step 1: Get a live link (5 minutes, free)</h2=
><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto"><strong>Easiest option =E2=80=94 Net=
lify Drop:</strong></div><ol start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=
=3D"auto">Go to <strong>app.netlify.com/drop</strong> and sign up free (Goo=
gle login works)</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Drag y=
our <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-i=
nline">dental_de_care.html</code> file onto the page</div></li><li><div cla=
ss=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Netlify instantly gives you a public URL =E2=
=80=94 send that link to your client via WhatsApp. It opens on any phone, n=
o app needed.</div></li></ol><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto"><strong>=
Alternative =E2=80=94 GitHub Pages</strong> (better if the client will edit=
 code):</div><ol start=3D"1"><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Crea=
te a free account at github.com =E2=86=92 New Repository =E2=86=92 name it =
anything</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Upload the HTM=
L file, rename it to <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=
=3D"segment-code-inline">index.html</code></div></li><li><div class=3D"para=
graph" dir=3D"auto">Settings =E2=86=92 Pages =E2=86=92 select the <code dat=
a-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">main</=
code> branch =E2=86=92 Save</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"a=
uto">GitHub gives you a free URL like <code data-v-bfaabce6=3D"" data-v-048=
cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">https://username.github.io/repo-na=
me/</code></div></li></ol><h2 class=3D"">Step 2: Let your client make chang=
es</h2><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Depends on how technical they =
are:</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto"><strong>If the client knows=
 a little code:</strong> the GitHub route is best. They edit the file right=
 on github.com (even from a phone browser), and the live site updates autom=
atically. No re-uploading.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto"><stro=
ng>If the client is non-technical:</strong> honestly, editing HTML on a pho=
ne is painful. The practical workflow is:</div><ul start=3D"1"><li><div cla=
ss=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Client opens the live link on their phone, no=
tes what they want changed ("make the phone number bigger", "add a whitenin=
g service")</div></li><li><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">They send y=
ou the feedback, you edit the file and re-drag it to Netlify (takes 30 seco=
nds) =E2=80=94 the link stays the same</div></li></ul><h2>One warning</h2><=
div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Don't just send the <code data-v-bfaab=
ce6=3D"" data-v-048cb31c=3D"" class=3D"segment-code-inline">.html</code> fi=
le over WhatsApp/email =E2=80=94 on iPhones it usually won't open, and on A=
ndroid it opens without styling half the time. Always share the <strong>hos=
ted link</strong> instead.</div><div class=3D"paragraph" dir=3D"auto">Want =
me to walk you through the Netlify or GitHub upload step by step?</div></di=
